Author: Pedro Cieza-Liza [aut, cre, cph],
    Reyniel Salas-Silva [aut],
    Jose Gamarra-Moncayo [aut, ctb]
Maintainer: Pedro Cieza-Liza <pedrocieza24@gmail.com>
Description: Provides a workflow for pre-data semantic screening and
    psychometric scale development that combines large language model item
    generation, semantic embeddings, ant colony optimization, sample-free
    proxy exploratory structural equation modeling with 'lavaan', dynamic
    fit-index calibration, pseudo-factor-analysis diagnostics, construct
    coverage diagnostics, empirical semantic-to-response calibration tools,
    and publication-ready visualizations. Sample-free semantic PFA, ESEM, and
    DFI outputs are explicitly treated as proxy diagnostics rather than
    participant-based evidence of construct validity. The package supports
    cloud and local model backends while keeping network-dependent examples
    optional during automated checks.
